    "body": "@annevk `make deploy` is [failing on CI](https://github.com/whatwg/compression/actions/runs/19097918742/job/54562418420). It looks like [this curl command](https://github.com/whatwg/whatwg.org/blob/f4844f60fc518ba4e644d5626ce90e3e3fa73773/resources.whatwg.org/build/deploy.sh#L158) is failing with an HTTP 404.\r\n\r\nDid GitHub change their URLs recently? Because [according to the docs](https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/releasing-projects-on-github/linking-to-releases#linking-to-the-latest-release) it should be this URL instead:\r\n```diff\r\n- curlretry --fail --remote-name --location https://github.com/validator/validator/releases/download/latest/vnu.linux.zip\r\n+ curlretry --fail --remote-name --location https://github.com/validator/validator/releases/latest/download/vnu.linux.zip\r\n```\r\nAnd that *does* work. 😅",
